keeping Claude working across turns until completion. Fast mode runs on Opus 4.7 by default. Rewind menu compresses context.\n   667→                </div>\n   668→                <div class=\"update-meta\">\n   669→                    <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n   670→                    <span>Claude Code</span>\n   671→                    <span>• 2026-05-08</span>\n   672→                </div>\n   673→            </div>\n   674→\n   675→            <div class=\"update-card\">\n   676→                <div class=\"update-title\">\n   677→                    <a href=\"https://releasebot.io/updates/google/gemini-cli\" target=\"_blank\">May 2026 Update</a>\n   678→                </div>\n   679→                <div class=\"update-description\">\n   680→                    Command line improvements, core and UI improvements, new session deletion options, commands listing, voice mode upgrades.\n   681→                </div>\n   682→                <div class=\"update-meta\">\n   683→                    <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n   684→                    <span>Gemini CLI</span>\n   685→                    <span>• 2026-05-08</span>\n   686→                </div>\n   687→            </div>\n   688→\n   689→            <div class=\"update-card\">\n   690→                <div class=\"update-title\">\n   691→                    <a href=\"https://cursor.sh/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Background Agent General Availability</a>\n   692→                </div>\n   693→                <div class=\"update-description\">\n   694→                    Cursor's remote coding agent now available to all users, enabling parallel task execution with cloud icon or Cmd/Ctrl+E.\n   695→                </div>\n   696→                <div class=\"update-meta\">\n   697→                    <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n   698→                    <span>Cursor</span>\n   699→                    <span>• 2026-05-08</span>\n   700→                </div>\n   701→            </div>\n   702→\n   703→            <div class=\"update-card\">\n   704→                <div class=\"update-title\">\n   705→                    <a href=\"https://windsurf.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Devin Review & Quick Review</a>\n   706→                </div>\n   707→                <div class=\"update-description\">\n   708→                    All Windsurf IDE users now have access to Devin Review and Quick Review. Devin Review available for self-serve users with 2 week free trial.\n   709→                </div>\n   710→                <div class=\"update-meta\">\n   711→                    <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n   712→                    <span>Windsurf</span>\n   713→                    <span>• 2026-05-06</span>\n   714→                </div>\n   715→            </div>\n   716→\n   717→            <div class=\"update-card\">\n   718→                <div class=\"update-title\">\n   719→                    <a href=\"https://cursor.sh/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Memories Feature Beta</a>\n   720→                </div>\n   721→                <div class=\"update-description\">\n   722→                    Memories beta allows AI to remember facts from conversations and reference them in future sessions, stored per project at individual level.\n   723→                </div>\n   724→                <div class=\"update-meta\">\n   725→                    <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n   726→                    <span>Cursor</span>\n   727→                    <span>• 2026-05-05</span>\n   728→                </div>\n   729→            </div>\n   730→        </section>\n   731→\n   732→        <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n   733→        <section class=\"technical-insights\" id=\"technical-insights\">\n   734→            <h2>Technical Insights</h2>\n   735→\n   736→            <div class=\"insight-card\">\n   737→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   738→                    <a href=\"https://www.windowscentral.com/microsoft/microsoft-cancels-claude-code-licenses-shifting-developers-to-github-copilot-cli-a-move-likely-driven-by-financial-motives\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Cancels Claude Code Licenses</a>\n   739→                </div>\n   740→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   741→                    Microsoft canceling Claude Code licenses for thousands of developers. Deadline June 30, 2026. Shifting to GitHub Copilot CLI due to spiraling AI costs.\n   742→                </div>\n   743→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   744→                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   745→                    <span>Windows Central</span>\n   746→                    <span>• 2026-05-24</span>\n   747→                </div>\n   748→            </div>\n   749→\n   750→            <div class=\"insight-card\">\n   751→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   752→                    <a href=\"https://kanbots.dev\" target=\"_blank\">Kanbots: Open Source Kanban AI Agents</a>\n   753→                </div>\n   754→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   755→                    v1.0 launched as MIT-licensed kanban running parallel Claude/Codex agents on every card. Autopilot mode, local-first, GitHub integration, MCP server.\n   756→                </div>\n   757→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   758→                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   759→                    <span>Hacker News</span>\n   760→                    <span>• 2026-05-24</span>\n   761→                </div>\n   762→            </div>\n   763→\n   764→            <div class=\"insight-card\">\n   765→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   766→                    <a href=\"https://deno.com/blog/v2.8\" target=\"_blank\">Deno 2.8 Released</a>\n   767→                </div>\n   768→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   769→                    Updates to JavaScript/TypeScript runtime with new features and improvements.\n   770→                </div>\n   771→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   772→                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   773→                    <span>Deno Team</span>\n   774→                    <span>• 2026-05-24</span>\n   775→                </div>\n   776→            </div>\n   777→\n   778→            <div class=\"insight-card\">\n   779→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   780→                    <a href=\"https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp\" target=\"_blank\">Bun Support Deprecated in yt-dlp</a>\n   781→                </div>\n   782→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   783→                    Bun support now limited and deprecated, reflecting ongoing challenges in JavaScript runtime ecosystem compatibility.\n   784→                </div>\n   785→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   786→                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   787→                    <span>yt-dlp Team</span>\n   788→                    <span>• 2026-05-24</span>\n   789→                </div>\n   790→            </div>\n   791→\n   792→            <div class=\"insight-card\">\n   793→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   794→                    <a href=\"https://github.com/superset-sh/superset\" target=\"_blank\">Superset: IDE for Agents Era</a>\n   795→                </div>\n   796→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   797→                    Launched from Y Combinator P26 as development environment designed for AI agent workflows.\n   798→                </div>\n   799→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   800→                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   801→                    <span>YC P26</span>\n   802→                    <span>• 2026-05-24</span>\n   803→                </div>\n   804→            </div>\n   805→\n   806→            <div class=\"insight-card\">\n   807→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   808→                    <a href=\"https://anthropic.com\" target=\"_blank\">Project Glasswing Update</a>\n   809→                </div>\n   810→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   811→                    Anthropic published initial update on Project Glasswing, trending on Hacker News with significant community interest.\n   812→                </div>\n   813→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   814→                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   815→                    <span>Anthropic</span>\n   816→                    <span>• 2026-05-24</span>\n   817→                </div>\n   818→            </div>\n   819→\n   820→            <div class=\"insight-card\">\n   821→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   822→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Memory Shortage: HBM Impact on Consumer Electronics</a>\n   823→                </div>\n   824→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   825→                    AI data centers causing memory shortages. HBM allocation increasing from 2% to 20% by end of 2026. HBM consumes 3x more wafer capacity per GB than DDR.\n   826→                </div>\n   827→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   828→                    <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   829→                    <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   830→                    <span>• 2026-05-22</span>\n   831→                </div>\n   832→            </div>\n   833→\n   834→            <div class=\"insight-card\">\n   835→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   836→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">FTC Settlement on AI Marketing Fraud</a>\n   837→                </div>\n   838→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   839→                    FTC announced firms will pay $1M to settle charges about deceiving customers on 'Active Listening' AI. Actually just resold email lists at markup.\n   840→                </div>\n   841→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   842→                    <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   843→                    <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   844→                    <span>• 2026-05-22</span>\n   845→                </div>\n   846→            </div>\n   847→\n   848→            <div class=\"insight-card\">\n   849→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   850→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Datasette Agent: First Release</a>\n   851→                </div>\n   852→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   853→                    Extensible AI assistant integrating LLM with Datasette. Runs commands in Fly Sprites sandbox, 'View SQL query' buttons, permission-based tools.\n   854→                </div>\n   855→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   856→                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   857→                    <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   858→                    <span>• 2026-05-21</span>\n   859→                </div>\n   860→            </div>\n   861→\n   862→            <div class=\"insight-card\">\n   863→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   864→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">SpaceX-Anthropic: $1.25B/Month Compute Deal</a>\n   865→                </div>\n   866→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   867→                    Anthropic paying $1.25 billion per month through May 2029 for SpaceX compute capacity. Capacity ramping in May-June 2026 at reduced fees.\n   868→                </div>\n   869→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   870→                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   871→                    <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   872→                    <span>• 2026-05-20</span>\n   873→                </div>\n   874→            </div>\n   875→\n   876→            <div class=\"insight-card\">\n   877→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   878→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">How Fast is 10 Tokens Per Second?</a>\n   879→                </div>\n   880→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   881→                    Interactive HTML app simulating LLM token output speeds from 5/second to 800/second, helping users understand what different speeds feel like.\n   882→                </div>\n   883→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   884→                    <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   885→                    <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   886→                    <span>• 2026-05-20</span>\n   887→                </div>\n   888→            </div>\n   889→\n   890→            <div class=\"insight-card\">\n   891→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   892→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Gemini 3.5 Flash: Prompt Injection Concerns</a>\n   893→                </div>\n   894→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   895→                    Google released Gemini 3.5 Flash and Gemini Spark agent. Simon concerned about prompt injection risks. Agent Gateway enforcing DLP policies in isolated VMs.\n   896→                </div>\n   897→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   898→                    <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   899→                    <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   900→                    <span>• 2026-05-20</span>\n   901→                </div>\n   902→            </div>\n   903→\n   904→            <div class=\"insight-card\">\n   905→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   906→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Gemini 3.5 Flash: More Expensive Strategy</a>\n   907→                </div>\n   908→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   909→                    Gemini 3.5 Flash went straight to GA without preview. Google using it across many key products. Discusses pricing implications and strategy.\n   910→                </div>\n   911→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   912→                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   913→                    <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   914→                    <span>• 2026-05-19</span>\n   915→                </div>\n   916→            </div>\n   917→\n   918→            <div class=\"insight-card\">\n   919→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   920→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Last Six Months in LLMs: PyCon Talk</a>\n   921→                </div>\n   922→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   923→                    Lightning talk at PyCon US 2026 with annotated slides covering last six months of LLM developments, rapid-fire overview of key trends.\n   924→                </div>\n   925→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   926→                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   927→                    <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   928→                    <span>• 2026-05-19</span>\n   929→                </div>\n   930→            </div>\n   931→\n   932→            <div class=\"insight-card\">\n   933→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   934→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">UK GDS on AI, Open Code, Vulnerability Risk</a>\n   935→                </div>\n   936→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   937→                    UK GDS published 'Keep open by default' guidance in response to NHS closing repos after vulnerability reports. Major escalation in civil service disagreement.\n   938→                </div>\n   939→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   940→                    <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   941→                    <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   942→                    <span>• 2026-05-17</span>\n   943→                </div>\n   944→            </div>\n   945→\n   946→            <div class=\"insight-card\">\n   947→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   948→                    <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=44095189\" target=\"_blank\">Ask HN: Struggling to get value from coding LLMs?</a>\n   949→                </div>\n   950→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   951→                    Discussion exploring developer frustration after deep testing of AI coding tools. Gap between hype and practical value.\n   952→                </div>\n   953→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   954→                    <span class=\"insight-type discussion\">Discussion</span>\n   955→                    <span>Hacker News</span>\n   956→                    <span>• 2026-05-18</span>\n   957→                </div>\n   958→            </div>\n   959→\n   960→            <div class=\"insight-card\">\n   961→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   962→                    <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=45727664\" target=\"_blank\">AI can code, but can't build software</a>\n   963→                </div>\n   964→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   965→                    'LLMs are remarkably good at writing code. Writing code isn't the same thing as delivering working software.' Gap between code generation and software delivery.\n   966→                </div>\n   967→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   968→                    <span class=\"insight-type discussion\">Discussion</span>\n   969→                    <span>Hacker News</span>\n   970→                    <span>• 2026-05-19</span>\n   971→                </div>\n   972→            </div>\n   973→\n   974→            <div class=\"insight-card\">\n   975→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   976→                    <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=44079303\" target=\"_blank\">Ask HN: Go deep into AI/LLMs or just use as tools?</a>\n   977→                </div>\n   978→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   979→                    Discussion on whether developers should specialize in AI/LLMs or use as productivity tools. Career strategy in age of AI assistants.\n   980→                </div>\n   981→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   982→                    <span class=\"insight-type discussion\">Discussion</span>\n   983→                    <span>Hacker News</span>\n   984→                    <span>• 2026-05-18</span>\n   985→                </div>\n   986→            </div>\n   987→\n   988→            <div class=\"insight-card\">\n   989→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   990→                    <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\" target=\"_blank\">ArXiv cs.AI and cs.LG Papers</a>\n   991→                </div>\n   992→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   993→                    Over 1,500 ML/AI papers submitted. Notable: 'GraphFlow' (ICML 2026), 'Vector Policy Optimization', 'Post-Training is About States', diffusion models, neural operators.\n   994→                </div>\n   995→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   996→                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   997→                    <span>ArXiv</span>\n   998→                    <span>• 2026-05-22</span>\n   999→                </div>\n  1000→            </div>\n  1001→        </section>\n  1002→    </main>\n  1003→\n  1004→    <footer>\n  1005→        <div class=\"container\">\n  1006→            <p>Generated by <a href=\"#\">Agent Cod